Files:
- index.html: website app
- manifest.webmanifest: installable web app metadata
- sw.js: offline cache service worker
- icon.svg: app icon

To use:
1. Upload all files together to an HTTPS static host (for example GitHub Pages or Netlify).
2. Open the published HTTPS website in Chrome on Android.
3. Use Chrome menu > Add to Home screen (or Install app if shown).

Important:
- Service workers and install prompts require HTTPS (localhost also works for testing).
- This is a settings guide only. It does not hack or modify Free Fire.
- The sensitivity numbers are suggested starting points, not guaranteed results
